ht also open and display a url. </p>
<ul class=3D"g-md-ul">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">If it does, do not close it until you are done workin=
g with Jupyter Notebook. </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">If it does not appear, don=E2=80=99t worry =E2=80=94 =
this has to do with your operating system and will not affect Jupyter Noteb=
ook=E2=80=99s performance.</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"terminal showing Jupyter Notebook running w=
ith directions to access the notebook in a browser" class=3D"g-md-img" src=
=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-science-career-path/get=
ting-started-off-platform/jupyter-terminal-running.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">When the notebook starts, you will be redirected to you=
r default browser, and you will see a list of all the folders your program =
will have access to. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can open a new Python file by selecting <kbd class=
=3D"g-md-kbd">New</kbd> &gt;&gt; <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Python3</kbd></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"launch Python3 from jupyter with command: p=
ython" class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths=
/data-science-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/open-new-python3.png=
"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">The new Notebook will open in a new tab. Click on the t=
itle to rename it.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image of an empty Jupyter notebook." class=
=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-scienc=
e-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/empty-jupyter-notebook.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">This is where you will write your code. You can write s=
mall or large chunks of code in each cell and run each cell independently o=
f others. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">To run a cell, you can use the <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">=
Run</kbd> button or <kbd class=3D"g-md-kbd">Shift</kbd> + <kbd class=3D"g-m=
d-kbd">Enter</kbd>.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"run button in the Jupyter Notebook menu" cl=
ass=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-sci=
ence-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/notebooks-function-bar-run.pn=
g"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">A new cell will appear after you run the cell you are w=
orking in. You can also add a new cell by clicking the <kbd class=3D"g-md-k=
bd">+</kbd> button at the top.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"+ button in the Jupyter Notebook menu" clas=
s=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-scien=
