 until then.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Let=E2=80=99s move on to one more supportive feature in=
 Jupyter Notebook: debugging.</p>
<h4 id=3D"heading-debugging-with-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-h4">Debugg=
ing with Jupyter Notebook</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Now let=E2=80=99s try to create an error. There is no p=
ackage named =E2=80=98panda=E2=80=99, but it is an easy typo to make. Let=
=E2=80=99s make that typo to see how Jupyter Notebook handles errors.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><code class=3D"g-md-code">import panda as pd</code></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">As expected, we got an error. Jupyter Notebook tries to=
 be as helpful as possible. There is a lot of information in this message, =
let=E2=80=99s break it down starting at the bottom. Our bottom line says: <=
/p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
